tions  about normalizing flows are still not  well understood  and that's the focus of our work  okay so first to set up what gans are so  gans are based on this game's theoretic  idea we have a generator who is  attempting to  imitate this natural distribution  so let's give it an adversary called the  discriminator who tries to distinguish  between the generated images and the  real images  and then this turns it into this min max  problem  okay so gans have enjoyed uh tremendous  success in creating photorealistic  images even with relatively small models  and they do allow efficient sampling  however they have some drawbacks  uh first training could be unstable  because it's this mid max problem it's  typically less stable than a pure  optimization problem  another problem is evaluation  we don't get access to a likelihood so  it's actually hard to evaluate how well  it fits the real distribution  so i'll introduce another approach  called normalizing flows  the idea here is to parametrize the  generator g to be invertible  this is a key restriction that allows  efficient computation of the likelihood  and this is because we can calculate by  the change of variables formula but  excessive formula for the probability  density  of any particular point  so we can see that's in terms of the  determinant of the jacobian of this map  and this means we can calculate the log  likelihood and then we can optimize it  by gradient ascent  however in this form it's still not  efficient enough  because calculating this determinant can  take a decubed time  so there's one more key ingredient here  to make it efficient  this brings us to the idea of affine  coupling normalizing flows  the idea is to restrict the form of g to  allow efficiently that is linear time  computable brilliance  and  this is  one of the  most successful methods in terms of  allowing normalizing flows to scale to  high resolution images  so skipping over some of the details  the idea is that we want to parametrize  the layers  of this neural network so that the  resulting jacobian is going to be  triangular  and this means that we can  calculate the  determinant simply as the product along  the diagonal  for the details this is an affine  coupling normalizing flow  half of the coordinates are copied at  each step and for the other half it's a  alkaline transformation given the  remaining coordinates  okay so flow models  can  resolve some of the drawbacks  that gans have in particular they allow  stabler training since we have the  likelihood objective that we're  maximizing  and it's also easier to evaluate  since we do have the likelihood function  harvard introduces some new issues  in particular needs to be larger  than the dam needs to be in order to  get the same performance uh and a major  problem is that  it can turn out to be ill-conditioned  during training uh jacobian could become  close to singular and  uh making the objective blow up  uh so  this point is what i'll focus on here  question is is this an inherent  difficulty or  something we could overcome  okay so a natural question is these two  is the question of which  which distributions can be represented  by well-conditioned affine coupling  normalizing flows  and i'll get this adjective from there  on and just call it normalization  so a series of recent works have uh  established universal approximation  uh particular colorado for uh alkaline  problem networks  however all these constructions are  poorly conditioned  so as the required accuracy epsilon goes  to zero the jacobian actually becomes  singular and this happens no matter how  nice the underlying distribution is  so our goal is to try and overcome this  and we show that in fact we have  universal approximation with uh  well-conditioned normalizing flows for a  large class of distributions by naming  logical distributions  so roughly our main theorem says that a  lot concave distribution with  conditional capital can be approximated  with a normalizing flow  uh with condition number that's  polynomial and capital  and for the details lot of concrete  distribution this is the hessian of the  log pdf is  a or the negative of this is a convex  function with condition numbers  so we actually consider a padded version  with iv gaussian variables  and  and by approximation here we mean that  for any approximation accuracy epsilon  we can get within epsilon in losses  distance  and as  the key point to note here is that  there's no dependence of the condition  number on the  accuracy epsilon  okay and uh it's also noted that  gaussian pattern has been empirically  noted to improve the condition  okay just a few words about the proof uh  two ingredients one is underdamped  longivian dynamics  sd used for sampling from the gibbs  distribution  and this produces a flow between the  target distribution and the standard  gaussian with good condition  and a second we showed that these  dynamics can be simulated by sequence of  what's called hanal like maps  actually a general generalization of  this  and then discretizing this dynamical  system then gives an alpha and conflict  so these are  kind of connected to synthetic different  life  okay so there's a lot of open questions  here so primary west can we relax the  assumption of law concavity it'd be nice  so we looked at the question of  representability but what i'd really  like to understand is optimization does  gradient descent find a good solution  and finally i would like to compare to  other generative models or the  separations between the different models  uh can make normalizing flows more  competitive and efficient  okay so that's it here's some of my  other work and feel free to talk to me  [Applause]  this is um new to me so i'm not sure if  this question will make any sense or not  but um so you know it is it is it  possible that you know maybe one  interpretation of this is you're trying  to find a good choice of obstacles  you're a good choice of transport mass  from for example a gaussian to your  desired target measure that has some you  know nice properties like most  polynomials  or things like that  and an obstacle is that the determinant  uh  could be  deteriorating um maybe along the  training dynamics and so i guess uh  one thing i was wondering is um you know  i know a lot full transport type of  things  is there any kind of appropriate analog  of that in this context  um  so i guess this in this this case is  okay so i think that's a really  interesting question if you're trying to  explore connections around that transfer  so this is a deterministic map from  you know telstra data  i guess  so  this is something contrasting with your  stochastic  stochastic map where you allow  randomness  um  and  i think  uh the deterministic natures are what  allows the easy complication of  likelihood

